{"version":"1","id":"ns","handle":"ns","name":"NativeScript","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/ns","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-2.1775,"y":-3.7629,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":63,"newest_post_at":"2020-05-12T15:33:29.000Z","oldest_post_at":"0123-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.039683,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.047619,"avg_read_time":0.0,"summary_length_avg":319.62963,"title_length_avg":50.047619,"title_length_var":196.204082,"tag_entropy":2.623574,"tag_diversity":0.52381,"top_tag_share":0.206349,"avg_upvotes":0.015873,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.015873,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":1.0,"zero_engagement_share":0.984127,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.682239,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.016129},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-9.0735,-4.1324],"cadence_depth":[-2.9706,-9.6765],"hype_variety":[7.6618,-5.5147],"title_style":[5.4853,-3.9265]},"top_tags":[["nativescript",56],["general-programming",17],["ios",11],["javascript",9],["apple",6],["webpack",6],["tech-news",6],["angular",5]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["\ud83c\udf89 Announcing @nativescript/capacitor Beta \ud83c\udf89","The Next Chapter for NativeScript: nStudio","Migration of NativeScript Cloud Builds to Circle CI"],"outlier":["Announcing NativeScript 6.0 - Webpack All The Way, Seamless App Updates, New Core Theme, and a Lot More"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"ebe4f38c4daf3a3caa35ecc9e1453075","title":"Migration of NativeScript Cloud Builds to Circle CI","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/migration-of-nativescript-cloud-builds-to-circle-ci","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/migration-of-nativescript-cloud-builds-to-circle-ci-ebe4f38c4daf3a3caa35ecc9e1453075","summary":"Existing NativeScript cloud builds will be stopped effectively on May 31st 2020. NativeScript-remote-builds plugin works with fastlane behind the scenes and relies on the fastlane match approach for iOS code signing. The plugin can be tuned to use different cloud providers or even a local machine. migrate to the new solution before this date!","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-05-12T15:33:29.000Z"},{"id":"e110917ee01e6b750046a8a216db3d42","title":"What's New in NativeScript 6.5","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/whats-new-in-nativescript-6-5","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-s-new-in-nativescript-6-5-e110917ee01e6b750046a8a216db3d42","summary":"NativeScript 6.5 is now available for iOS. The Tabs and BottomNavigation components were introduced as beta components in 6.1. With this release, both components are further expanding their functionality by providing means for creating them programmatically. Two new properties for the TabStrip component: selectedItemColor and unSelectedItemColor.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-03-18T19:48:42.000Z"},{"id":"7a284d766fefadc548dc8c28e0b94f75","title":"Protecting Your Source Code with Jscrambler","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/protecting-your-source-code-with-jscrambler","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/protecting-your-source-code-with-jscrambler-7a284d766fefadc548dc8c28e0b94f75","summary":"Jscrambler is a premium security tool that transforms the JavaScript in your application to make it extremely difficult to reverse engineer. Because JavaScript is not a compiled language, your NativeScript application\u2019s source code gets distributed in plain text as part of your Android and iOS application packages. Watch the webinar \"Best Practices for Securing Your Mobile Apps\" to get some tips and tricks on NativeScript security.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-03-05T16:02:34.000Z"},{"id":"2394371b3bc0d605940923816dcc325b","title":"Secure Your Mobile App - Episode One (Protecting the Code)","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/secure-your-mobile-app-protecting-the-code","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/secure-your-mobile-app---episode-one-protecting-the-code--2394371b3bc0d605940923816dcc325b","summary":"Mobile security is something that can no longer be taken lightly. Most of these are incredibly easy to implement, as the heavy lifting has already been managed by our illustrious community of plugin developers. NativeScript, React Native, and Cordova/Ionic are not compiled to native byte code. Minification/obfuscation is the least powerful method of securing your code.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-03-05T16:02:28.000Z"},{"id":"5a84688e27fd58a1a49b4731a06df07d","title":"Build NativeScript Apps Remotely from Windows or Linux","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/build-nativescript-apps-remotely-from-windows-or-linux","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/build-nativescript-apps-remotely-from-windows-or-linux-5a84688e27fd58a1a49b4731a06df07d","summary":"The NativeScript Remote Builds plugin enables the existing NativeScript. commands on environments without any native tooling requirements. The plugin is designed to be stable and reliable in a CI environement. It is available only through NativeScript Sidekick. iOS signing management. It provides a limited number of free Android Builds and free iOS builds.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-03-04T13:52:57.000Z"},{"id":"82f9a762fcc71d64d1130d119725c4c5","title":"NativeScript 6.4 Has Just Landed","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/nativescript-6.4-has-just-landed","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/nativescript-6-4-has-just-landed-82f9a762fcc71d64d1130d119725c4c5","summary":"NativeScript 6.4.0 is now available on all major platforms. New features include custom webpack configuration and support for WebAssembly on Android. 3D rotations are now available in NativeScript. NativeScript now has support for pnpm, a package manager for the command line.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-02-12T15:07:31.000Z"},{"id":"44a10eb37f9a74c9247b94d786f83b06","title":"New V8-based iOS Runtime is Now in BETA","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/new-v8-based-ios-runtime-is-now-in-beta","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-v8-based-ios-runtime-is-now-in-beta-44a10eb37f9a74c9247b94d786f83b06","summary":"The team is working on total revamp of the iOS runtime. The goal is to use the V8 engine instead of JavaScriptCore. Several months ago, the team shipped an alpha version of this runtime. Now it\u2019s time to announce the next iteration. The new iOS runtime is feature complete and relatively stable.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-01-15T22:16:55.000Z"},{"id":"1113088d6123677ee3115e8bf3c49092","title":"NativeScript 6.3 - The Holiday Edition","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/nativescript-6.3-the-holiday-edition","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/nativescript-6-3---the-holiday-edition-1113088d6123677ee3115e8bf3c49092","summary":"6.3 brings a brand new CSS Parser, which provides up to 30% faster startup time according to our tests. In 6.3, developers can use the scoped packages like @nativescript/core, @nativecript/angular, etc. without the need to install the older packages as well.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2019-12-19T18:05:46.000Z"},{"id":"848e12f61fcb93db6c7e6c307aca35d9","title":"Your NativeScript UpLabs Challenge Winners","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/your-nativescript-uplabs-challenge-winners","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/your-nativescript-uplabs-challenge-winners-848e12f61fcb93db6c7e6c307aca35d9","summary":"NativeScript and UpLabs collaborated on a \"challenge\" to inspire designers and developers to collaborate on building engaging apps with NativeScript. We received some great submissions, the community voted, and now it's time to award some prizes. The first prize was awarded via an internal vote of folks on the NativeScript team.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2019-12-05T14:39:35.000Z"},{"id":"ac72fa478b4787992d6b775777a7afdb","title":"Detecting Shakes in NativeScript","url":"https://www.nativescript.org/blog/detecting-shakes-in-nativescript","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/detecting-shakes-in-nativescript-ac72fa478b4787992d6b775777a7afdb","summary":"In this blog we are going to learn how to detect a \"shake\" gesture in NativeScript apps. We will use the nativescript-accelerometer plugin to start listening to accelerometer data. The ShakeDetector implementation will detect a shake if: 3 readings ( SHAKE_COUNT ) are separated by 800ms. If all three conditions are met, we will call the callback and wait for 1 second before firing the event again.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/518bfe31fa2289f1d9a0731e1cf3e3ab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2019-12-03T16:49:04.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["regehr","80lv","koaning","robohub","devtech"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id"